1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,325
The Dead Sea Scrolls.

2
00:00:02,275 --> 00:00:11,162
In 1947, a Bedouin shepherd searching for a lost goat discovered clay jars in a cave near the Dead Sea, containing ancient scrolls.

3
00:00:11,162 --> 00:00:20,462
Subsequent excavations across 11 caves yielded thousands of parchment and papyrus fragments dating from the 3rd century BCE to the 1st century CE.

4
00:00:20,462 --> 00:00:30,750
The scrolls include the oldest known copies of the Hebrew Bible, over 1,000 years older than any previously known manuscripts, alongside previously unknown religious texts.

5
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:36,675
The scrolls were likely hidden by the Essenes, a Jewish sect, during a period of conflict.

6
00:00:36,675 --> 00:00:43,575
They transformed understanding of biblical textual development and revealed the diversity of Second Temple Judaism.

